:tipage.
:edition title='First Edition (October 2026)'.
:p.This edition describes VM/370plus as it stands on 14 October 2026:
kit build 16 and the work in progress after it. It replaces no other
publication. The VM/370plus Guide (VMP-0001) remains the manual for
installing and using the system; this book says what is finished, what
is being worked on, what is known to be wrong and what comes next.
:p.VM/370plus is a hobbyist project. It is not a product of, and this
book is not a publication of, International Business Machines
Corporation. IBM, System/370, ESA/390, z/Architecture and VM/370 are
names of IBM products and architectures, used here only to identify
the systems this software runs on and descends from.
:p.The milestone plan (docs/VM370PLUS-Milestones.xlsx), the issue
register (docs/13-ISSUES.md) and the test runs in the project
repository are the sources of every statement in this book.
:eedition.
:toc.
:h1.About This Book
:p.This book is a snapshot. It is written for people who follow the
project, test its kits or want to decide what to try next. It assumes
you know VM/370: CP, CMS, the user directory and the Hercules
emulator. It does not repeat the installation and usage material of
the VM/370plus Guide.
:p.The chapters follow the areas of the milestone plan:
:ul.
:li.:hp2.Summary&colon.:ehp2. the whole system on one page.
:li.:hp2.The Control Program&colon.:ehp2. the ESA/390 conversion of CP,
real storage, and the virtual machines CP offers.
:li.:hp2.CMS&colon.:ehp2. the EC-mode CMS, storage above 16 MB and the
large-minidisk file system.
:li.:hp2.Linux Guests&colon.:ehp2. Linux/390 and Debian under CP.
:li.:hp2.Languages and Tools&colon.:ehp2. compilers, interpreters and
utilities on CMS and in the Debian guest.
:li.:hp2.Networking and Services&colon.:ehp2. the spool bridge, sockets,
messaging, and the guest LAN now being built.
:li.:hp2.Documents and Printing&colon.:ehp2. troff, BookMaster, LaTeX,
Ghostscript and printers.
:li.:hp2.The Kit&colon.:ehp2. what build 16 contains.
:li.:hp2.Known Problems&colon.:ehp2. the open issues that matter.
:li.:hp2.Plan&colon.:ehp2. what comes next.
:eul.
:p.Status words are used in one sense only. :hp2.Done:ehp2. means the
function was tested on a running system and, unless stated, shipped in
a kit. :hp2.In progress:ehp2. means work has started and partial
results exist. :hp2.Planned:ehp2. means agreed but not started.
:body.
:h1.Summary
:p.VM/370plus is the VM/370 Community Edition V1 R1.2 with its Control
Program converted from System/370 to ESA/390. CP runs in 31-bit
addressing mode under Hercules with ARCHMODE ESA/390. It still runs
every S/370 virtual machine that CE runs, and it adds two kinds of
virtual machine that VM/370 never had: 31-bit CMS machines larger than
16 MB, and ESA/390 virtual machines that run Linux/390.
:p.On 14 October 2026 the position is:
:fig.
