:etable.
:figcap.Parts of kit build 16
:efig.
:p.What each build added is listed in README-VM370PLUS.TXT in part 1.
Builds 14 to 16 added PostgreSQL 16, MQ for CMS, the Debian terminal
fix, Java and NetRexx, and the CP storage fixes.
:h1.Known Problems
:p.The issue register has every problem found since the conversion
began. These are the open ones that a user of build 16 can meet, or
that block the next steps:
:fig.
:table cols='5 28'.
:thd.
:row.
:c.Issue
:c.Description
:ethd.
:row.
:c.I-292
:c.Guest LAN: CP fails when two members exchange frames; after the
automatic re-IPL CP loops on the busy 0009 console. Not in a kit.
:row.
:c.I-291
:c.A dedicated LCS device cannot run under CP (suspend and resume in
translated channel programs). Superseded by the guest LAN.
:row.
:c.I-287
:c.Two Linux guests coupled by virtual CTCAs: CP stops dispatching.
Linux-to-Linux virtual CTCAs do not connect yet.
:row.
:c.I-284
:c.Once, CP's IPL ended in Hercules machine checks (host signal);
not reproduced.
:row.
:c.I-279
:c.Once, a CP PRG005 system failure while a 2 MB user ran out of
storage and Debian was busy; not reproduced.
:row.
:c.I-253
:c.CP SPOOL PUNCH TO SYSTEM answers INVALID OPTION (cosmetic).
:row.
:c.I-251
:c.CPWATCH does not run (worked around; milestone 4c).
:etable.
:figcap.Open issues
:efig.
:p.Two restrictions are by design: the console line of a Linux user
must be re-enabled from OPERATOR after a dropped connection (VARY
ONLINE and ENABLE), and CMS under IPL CMS keeps the 16 MB and 800-byte
block limits of VM/370.
:h1.Plan
:p.The order of the next work:
:ol.
:li.Finish the guest LAN: fix I-292, ping between two guests, cleanup
at DETACH and LOGOFF (9.12b); then the BORDER firewall (9.12c) and
DHCP/DNS (9.12d). A kit follows, with the Guide updated.
:li.cREXX natively on CMS: RXBVM82 (8.2).
:li.CPWATCH (4c), ooRexx 5 in Debian (9.9), the public VM/370 tools
(9.13), mail (9.18), a tiny LLM on CMS (9.17) and an AI gateway
service machine (9.10).
:li.z/Architecture: CP in 64-bit mode, with a migration guide (M10).
:li.Multiprocessing, more languages, VoIP, IoT, containers (M11).
:li.DOS/VS Release 34 and MVS 3.8j (TK5) as guests (M12, M13).
:eol.
:p.The milestone sheet in the repository is kept current after every
unit of work; this book is a picture of one day.
:euserdoc.
